  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating access to Prevention, Treatment and Home Based care for malaria and increasing the access to Affordable ACTs in the Private Sector - Mauritius (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritius, HIV, Ministry of Health and Wellness (MOH &amp; W)This program has the following goals: Reduction in AIDS-related mortality.  Stabilization of HIV prevalence among Key Population (PWID, MSM, TG and Sex Workers). The objectives of this program are: Provide ART to 70% of PLHIV eligible for ART; Ensure 90% of PLHIV on ART adherent after 12 months.  Provide voluntary HIV testing to 60% of combined mapped key populations.  Reach 30% of mapped transgendered people with HIV prevention education and materials; Reach 50% of mapped sex workers with HIV prevention education and materials; Provide voluntary HIV testing to 60% of combined mapped key populations.  Reach 45% of mapped MSM with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reach 50% of mapped sex workers with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reach 80% of mapped PWID with HIV prevention education and materials</narrative>
  </description>
